James sought assistance in rewording a statement in his paper regarding the economic damages associated with CO2 emissions. He needed clarification on whether the estimated $360 per ton of CO2 damage accounted for impacts on marginalized groups. I provided three options for rephrasing: 

1. Emphasizing that the estimates incorporate the disproportionate impacts on marginalized groups.
2. Using "included vs additional" language to clarify that the estimate includes these impacts, which typically underestimate total damages.
3. Describing the consequences of excluding marginalized group impacts, indicating that these values could be 10–30% higher with such omissions. 

I also offered to tune the phrasing to fit the surrounding context if provided.
